1
00:00:24,831 --> 00:00:25,961
Oh! I saw a flash.

2
00:00:29,751 --> 00:00:31,671
-Hey!
-What's that?

3
00:00:47,521 --> 00:00:48,731
Oh, really?

4
00:00:48,811 --> 00:00:50,941
Then this is where we say goodbye.

5
00:00:51,031 --> 00:00:53,191
I'm in a hurry. Excuse me.

6
00:01:13,551 --> 00:01:16,551
Don't put on airs, you grunts.

7
00:01:18,141 --> 00:01:19,351
If you want to leave,

8
00:01:19,431 --> 00:01:23,101
then go wash your ass in that river
and line up for Thorkell.

9
00:01:24,101 --> 00:01:26,561
That's all you need do.

10
00:01:26,641 --> 00:01:30,311
What Thorkell wants is the prince's ass.

11
00:01:31,731 --> 00:01:32,731
Hey, Askeladd.

12
00:01:33,731 --> 00:01:37,111
We've known each other for a long time.
I don't want to kill you.

13
00:01:37,201 --> 00:01:39,991
Leave the prince here and disappear.

14
00:03:27,811 --> 00:03:28,641
Avalon?

15
00:03:31,351 --> 00:03:33,021
Is that the name of a place?

16
00:03:33,101 --> 00:03:34,731
SERVANT

17
00:03:34,811 --> 00:03:36,361
Yes.

18
00:03:36,441 --> 00:03:38,441
It's the name of heaven.

19
00:03:39,491 --> 00:03:42,661
Our great ancestor, King Artorius,

20
00:03:43,661 --> 00:03:45,321
is over there.

21
00:03:48,831 --> 00:03:52,291
But, Mother... King Artorius

22
00:03:52,371 --> 00:03:54,331
is a general from a long time ago.

23
00:03:56,251 --> 00:03:57,631
Is he still alive?

24
00:04:02,841 --> 00:04:04,721
Avalon

25
00:04:04,801 --> 00:04:08,311
lies far across the great sea to the west.

26
00:04:08,391 --> 00:04:11,931
It's a land of everlasting spring, where the fairies live.

27
00:04:12,941 --> 00:04:17,111
It's a place free from the suffering
of death and old age in this life.

28
00:04:17,191 --> 00:04:19,021
He's recovering

29
00:04:19,111 --> 00:04:21,821
from his battle wounds there.

30
00:04:24,451 --> 00:04:28,741
Once his wounds have healed, King Artorius

31
00:04:28,831 --> 00:04:31,831
will come back for us.

32
00:04:32,831 --> 00:04:35,751
To save us from our suffering.

33
00:04:40,841 --> 00:04:42,461
When that happens,

34
00:04:43,471 --> 00:04:46,011
serve the king.

35
00:04:47,221 --> 00:04:48,971
He's

36
00:04:49,051 --> 00:04:51,471
the true king, and a warrior.

37
00:04:54,351 --> 00:04:56,901
Become his staff

38
00:04:56,981 --> 00:04:58,231
and his sword...

39
00:04:59,771 --> 00:05:01,151
someday.

40
00:05:06,661 --> 00:05:08,281
Can I talk to you

41
00:05:08,371 --> 00:05:10,201
before we say goodbye?

42
00:05:11,201 --> 00:05:13,121
It won't change anything.

43
00:05:13,201 --> 00:05:17,671
We've been together for a long time.

44
00:05:18,881 --> 00:05:20,711
We laughed together,

45
00:05:20,791 --> 00:05:22,881
we drank together,

46
00:05:22,961 --> 00:05:26,381
and we made it through hell and back many times.

47
00:05:30,301 --> 00:05:32,811
I've never told you this before.

48
00:05:34,021 --> 00:05:37,941
For the last decade we've spent together...

49
00:05:40,771 --> 00:05:42,821
I actually

50
00:05:42,901 --> 00:05:44,991
hated you guys.

51
00:05:45,991 --> 00:05:48,071
-What?
-What?

52
00:05:48,161 --> 00:05:51,081
You worthless Danes. You're worse than pigs.

53
00:06:00,291 --> 00:06:03,381
Damn! Get the prince!

54
00:06:05,421 --> 00:06:06,341
Thorfinn!

55
00:06:15,811 --> 00:06:18,391
You kids, hold on tight!

56
00:06:18,481 --> 00:06:19,651
Hurry!

57
00:06:21,311 --> 00:06:23,481
Damn!

58
00:06:23,571 --> 00:06:25,981
Damn! They were on to us!

59
00:06:26,071 --> 00:06:28,491
Follow them! Don't let them get away!

60
00:06:28,571 --> 00:06:30,991
Go! Go! Go!

61
00:06:31,071 --> 00:06:34,081
All right! I won't let you!

62
00:06:36,371 --> 00:06:39,791
The river! Follow the sled! Go!

63
00:06:43,881 --> 00:06:47,881
My men are impressive.
They're good at judging the situation.

64
00:06:50,091 --> 00:06:51,721
Very well.

65
00:06:57,851 --> 00:06:59,941
You got me.

66
00:07:02,231 --> 00:07:05,271
It looks like you didn't have enough faith.

67
00:07:12,491 --> 00:07:14,531
They're far away. I can't see them well.

68
00:07:15,531 --> 00:07:17,661
But it looks like they're fighting.

69
00:07:18,831 --> 00:07:20,371
They're fighting amongst themselves.

70
00:07:20,461 --> 00:07:22,501
It happens a lot in times like this.

71
00:07:22,581 --> 00:07:24,461
How pitiful.

72
00:07:24,541 --> 00:07:25,541
These days

73
00:07:25,631 --> 00:07:27,551
everyone's afraid to die.

74
00:07:28,551 --> 00:07:32,261
This is outrageous!

75
00:07:32,341 --> 00:07:35,221
How dare they start the fight without me?

76
00:07:35,301 --> 00:07:36,141
That's his problem?

77
00:07:36,221 --> 00:07:38,311
Let me join! Let me join!

78
00:07:46,231 --> 00:07:47,611
Surround them! Surround them!

79
00:07:47,691 --> 00:07:49,441
The horses! Kill their horses!

80
00:07:55,741 --> 00:07:58,161
What are you doing? Kill them, Thorfinn!

81
00:07:58,241 --> 00:07:59,491
Throw your knives!

82
00:07:59,581 --> 00:08:01,661
Shut up! I'm out of throwing knives!

83
00:08:02,661 --> 00:08:05,421
Damn! Askeladd's not here yet!

84
00:08:05,501 --> 00:08:07,171
What is that baldy doing?

85
00:08:09,211 --> 00:08:12,421
Stop, Bjorn! Listen to us!

86
00:08:12,511 --> 00:08:15,761
You think I'm stupid enough to actually stop?

87
00:08:15,841 --> 00:08:16,931
Don't forget who I am!

88
00:08:19,011 --> 00:08:22,811
Think about it, Bjorn! Whether we live or die

89
00:08:22,891 --> 00:08:25,561
all depends on what we do with the prince!

90
00:08:25,651 --> 00:08:30,031
It's no use, Atli! Bjorn obeys Askeladd completely.

91
00:08:30,111 --> 00:08:31,611
We can't convince him.

92
00:08:31,691 --> 00:08:33,321
We'll just have to kill him!

93
00:08:33,401 --> 00:08:37,201
Yeah. Looks like you do understand.

94
00:08:37,281 --> 00:08:40,201
Askeladd trusts me.
That's why he left the prince with me.

95
00:08:40,291 --> 00:08:42,701
If you want to take the prince from me,

96
00:08:42,791 --> 00:08:44,871
prepare to die!

97
00:08:44,961 --> 00:08:46,711
You cowards!

98
00:08:46,791 --> 00:08:50,131
Hey! I told you to attack me!

99
00:08:50,211 --> 00:08:53,381
Not the horses! No! Hey!

100
00:08:53,471 --> 00:08:54,721
We're going to crash!

101
00:09:18,281 --> 00:09:22,741
-Hey! Thorfinn's running away!
-Don't worry about him. Forget it.

102
00:09:22,831 --> 00:09:24,581
Hey, prince. Are you alive?

103
00:09:24,661 --> 00:09:26,421
Don't be so reckless!

104
00:09:26,501 --> 00:09:27,671
Prince! Hey!

105
00:09:31,751 --> 00:09:33,801
He's alive.

106
00:09:33,881 --> 00:09:35,921
All right! Let's go back.

107
00:09:41,471 --> 00:09:43,721
You're not going anywhere yet,

108
00:09:43,811 --> 00:09:45,891
you losers!

109
00:09:46,891 --> 00:09:49,651
You're still alive, Bjorn?

110
00:09:49,731 --> 00:09:51,521
What? That mushroom!

111
00:09:51,611 --> 00:09:54,361
Come at me, all of you at once!

112
00:09:56,151 --> 00:09:59,201
I'll take you all to Valhalla!

113
00:10:02,531 --> 00:10:04,751
Damn! Damn! Damn!

114
00:10:04,831 --> 00:10:07,461
You put me through so much trouble! You baldy!

115
00:10:07,541 --> 00:10:10,961
You better not die until I kill you,

116
00:10:11,041 --> 00:10:12,591
Askeladd!

117
00:10:26,561 --> 00:10:28,561
Oh, dear.

118
00:10:28,641 --> 00:10:31,101
I don't like getting old.

119
00:10:32,191 --> 00:10:34,521
Who ever thought

120
00:10:34,611 --> 00:10:38,031
that I'd be unable to escape
from a mere 50 men one day?

121
00:11:06,061 --> 00:11:07,431
Wait for it.

122
00:11:07,521 --> 00:11:09,141
Wait for your chance to escape.

123
00:11:20,781 --> 00:11:22,991
Thorkell's going to get here soon.

124
00:11:23,991 --> 00:11:25,621
It's going to be chaos.

125
00:11:34,041 --> 00:11:36,921
You bastard!

126
00:11:45,351 --> 00:11:46,851
Did you see that?

127
00:11:46,931 --> 00:11:48,061
I saw it.

128
00:11:48,141 --> 00:11:49,391
He cut through his helmet.

129
00:11:49,471 --> 00:11:51,731
Not even my ax can cut like that.

130
00:11:51,811 --> 00:11:54,651
Damn. He's good.

131
00:11:59,321 --> 00:12:03,071
Damn. I shouldn't have lost my temper.

132
00:12:05,661 --> 00:12:09,121
Oh, sorry I was being loud.

133
00:12:09,201 --> 00:12:10,661
All right. Come on.

134
00:12:10,751 --> 00:12:13,621
I'm not mad anymore.

135
00:12:21,471 --> 00:12:25,181
Everyone to the east, stand back!
You're going to get hit by the stray arrows!

136
00:12:26,761 --> 00:12:29,641
They took out their flying toys.

137
00:12:32,981 --> 00:12:34,731
Torgrim.

138
00:12:34,811 --> 00:12:36,521
Are you the one in charge?

139
00:12:36,611 --> 00:12:39,361
So what if I am? You bastard.

140
00:12:39,441 --> 00:12:42,781
Are you sure you're okay with this?
Even I would die from that.

141
00:12:42,861 --> 00:12:44,611
Who cares?

142
00:12:44,701 --> 00:12:47,161
Bjorn and Thorfinn are good.

143
00:12:47,241 --> 00:12:50,161
They'll kill you if you go after them.

144
00:12:50,241 --> 00:12:51,751
If you want to get the prince,

145
00:12:51,831 --> 00:12:54,581
you'll need me.

146
00:12:55,961 --> 00:12:58,961
If you take me hostage,

147
00:12:59,041 --> 00:13:02,961
then Bjorn will come back to exchange me for the prince.

148
00:13:03,051 --> 00:13:05,511
That's only if I'm still alive, though.

149
00:13:08,261 --> 00:13:09,971
What are you going to do, Torgrim?

150
00:13:11,221 --> 00:13:12,271
Aim for his legs.

151
00:13:18,311 --> 00:13:19,271
Yeah!

152
00:13:19,361 --> 00:13:20,981
We did it!

153
00:13:35,041 --> 00:13:37,331
You're not acting like yourself, Askeladd.

154
00:13:38,631 --> 00:13:42,001
You were never this desperate.

155
00:13:42,091 --> 00:13:46,591
Normally, you'd avoid fighting
worthless battles.

156
00:13:47,591 --> 00:13:51,301
Why do you risk your life for that coward of a prince?

157
00:13:51,391 --> 00:13:54,391
Do you plan on taking your prize to the grave with you?

158
00:14:01,061 --> 00:14:03,731
I'm already old.

159
00:14:03,821 --> 00:14:07,201
I don't have a lot of time left
where I can still work.

160
00:14:10,071 --> 00:14:11,621
I just...

161
00:14:13,411 --> 00:14:15,621
couldn't wait any longer.

162
00:14:19,831 --> 00:14:21,081
I couldn't wait anymore

163
00:14:22,291 --> 00:14:26,051
for the true king to return from Avalon.

164
00:14:44,821 --> 00:14:46,611
You don't make any sense.

165
00:14:47,611 --> 00:14:49,491
That's enough. Finish him.

166
00:14:51,951 --> 00:14:53,281
Hey! What's wrong?

167
00:15:00,171 --> 00:15:04,091
Hey! Are you having fun, guys?

168
00:15:06,171 --> 00:15:10,051
Which one is Askeladd? Your leader.

169
00:15:10,131 --> 00:15:13,011
I can't wait to meet him.

170
00:15:15,431 --> 00:15:16,641
Too bad.

171
00:15:19,181 --> 00:15:21,941
I don't see anyone without an appointment.

172
00:15:46,171 --> 00:15:48,341
You really are big.

173
00:15:49,551 --> 00:15:51,221
Now that I've seen you up close.

174
00:15:57,681 --> 00:16:00,101
I'm Torgrim.

175
00:16:00,181 --> 00:16:04,021
I'm not going to resist. I just want you to listen.

176
00:16:15,031 --> 00:16:17,741
Captain. The prince isn't here.

177
00:16:18,991 --> 00:16:20,701
Oh, that's right!

178
00:16:20,791 --> 00:16:23,001
That's what I was going to talk to you about.

179
00:16:23,081 --> 00:16:27,001
We were planning to give you the prince.

180
00:16:27,091 --> 00:16:31,671
But our leader Askeladd let him get away.

181
00:16:31,761 --> 00:16:33,381
But don't worry.

182
00:16:33,471 --> 00:16:36,391
We sent ten men after him.

183
00:16:36,471 --> 00:16:40,141
Just leave it to us.

184
00:16:40,221 --> 00:16:44,141
I swear in the name of Odin.
We'll get him back, no matter what.

185
00:16:44,231 --> 00:16:47,731
We also have other aces up our sleeve.

186
00:16:47,811 --> 00:16:49,901
What? Wait... Hey!

187
00:16:55,571 --> 00:16:58,121
So, you're Askeladd.

188
00:16:58,201 --> 00:17:00,621
You look pretty smart.

189
00:17:03,411 --> 00:17:05,081
By the way,

190
00:17:05,171 --> 00:17:08,211
I don't see Thorfinn around.

191
00:17:08,291 --> 00:17:10,041
Did you kill him?

192
00:17:11,251 --> 00:17:13,051
I didn't kill him.

193
00:17:13,131 --> 00:17:15,341
I asked him to guard the prince.

194
00:17:15,431 --> 00:17:18,261
He's not part of this rebellion.

195
00:17:18,341 --> 00:17:22,351
I see! I'm relieved to hear that.

196
00:17:25,021 --> 00:17:29,481
All right! Thanks for waiting, you dogs!

197
00:17:31,271 --> 00:17:33,741
Except for Askeladd,

198
00:17:33,821 --> 00:17:35,531
kill them all!

199
00:17:45,831 --> 00:17:48,541
This wasn't part of the deal, Torgrim!

200
00:17:48,631 --> 00:17:50,881
Hey, you guys.

201
00:17:50,961 --> 00:17:54,711
Pick up your weapons. Act like a warrior
for your final moments.

202
00:17:57,551 --> 00:18:00,011
Hurry up. Pick it up.

203
00:18:00,091 --> 00:18:02,851
I'm saying this for your own good.

204
00:18:02,931 --> 00:18:06,891
You won't be able to go to Valhalla if you die
without a weapon.

205
00:18:13,901 --> 00:18:16,651
Damn it all!

206
00:18:25,831 --> 00:18:28,541
Great. This is how it's supposed to be.

207
00:18:28,621 --> 00:18:30,421
Wait! Wait, Thorkell!

208
00:18:30,501 --> 00:18:32,881
Are you sure? Are you sure about this?

209
00:18:32,961 --> 00:18:35,921
If you kill us, you won't be able to get the prince!

210
00:18:36,011 --> 00:18:39,341
Yeah. That's okay. I'll get him myself.

211
00:18:42,051 --> 00:18:44,811
Hey. It's your ax.

212
00:18:44,891 --> 00:18:46,981
Attack me!

213
00:18:47,061 --> 00:18:50,481
If you call yourself a warrior, then try feeling good
when you die.

214
00:18:57,151 --> 00:19:02,031
One, two, three, four.
Two, two, three, four...

215
00:19:02,121 --> 00:19:04,661
I feel your pain, Torgrim.

216
00:19:04,741 --> 00:19:06,621
-My heart--
-Silence!

217
00:19:06,701 --> 00:19:08,711
It's all your fault!

218
00:19:10,041 --> 00:19:13,501
Just give up, Torgrim.

219
00:19:13,591 --> 00:19:15,461
You're going to die now.

220
00:19:16,711 --> 00:19:18,881
You're going to die without a doubt.

221
00:19:21,431 --> 00:19:25,601
So, die while fighting. Okay?

222
00:19:25,681 --> 00:19:27,811
I'll help you.

223
00:19:30,391 --> 00:19:33,651
Now then! Attack me! Come on!

224
00:19:34,691 --> 00:19:35,611
Hey!

225
00:19:53,041 --> 00:19:54,541
This is no good!

226
00:19:55,541 --> 00:19:58,131
Looks like I put too much pressure on you.

227
00:20:00,381 --> 00:20:01,971
This is no good.

228
00:20:02,051 --> 00:20:04,011
He's gone now.

229
00:20:05,181 --> 00:20:06,431
Hello?

230
00:20:19,281 --> 00:20:20,281
What's that?

231
00:20:35,291 --> 00:20:36,671
Thorfinn!

232
00:21:08,741 --> 00:21:11,661
Hey! Thorfinn!
You look like you've been doing well!

233
00:21:11,741 --> 00:21:13,711
Don't touch Askeladd!

234
00:21:13,791 --> 00:21:16,461
He's my catch!

235
00:21:16,541 --> 00:21:19,841
If you lay even one finger on him, I'm going to kill you!

236
00:21:19,921 --> 00:21:23,841
Got it, big guy? If you touch him, I'm going to kill you!

237
00:21:26,341 --> 00:21:30,181
I... I always knew you were crazy, but...

238
00:21:31,851 --> 00:21:35,391
A mouse is picking a fight with a bear.

239
00:21:40,771 --> 00:21:42,191
Your catch?

240
00:21:42,281 --> 00:21:44,691
He's your boss, right?

241
00:21:44,781 --> 00:21:46,701
He's not my boss!

242
00:21:46,781 --> 00:21:50,201
What? What the heck?

243
00:21:50,281 --> 00:21:54,081
Did you hear that? That kid said
he's going to kill our captain.

244
00:21:54,161 --> 00:21:56,961
Oh, he has a lot of guts to say that.

245
00:21:58,621 --> 00:22:01,591
Give me Askeladd.

246
00:22:01,671 --> 00:22:03,801
If you don't, I'm going to kill you.

247
00:22:03,881 --> 00:22:05,671
Really?

248
00:22:05,761 --> 00:22:08,431
Then I'm not going to.

249
00:22:08,511 --> 00:22:10,301
Did you hear that?

250
00:22:10,391 --> 00:22:12,681
Thorfinn and I just agreed

251
00:22:12,761 --> 00:22:16,431
to a duel over Askeladd!

252
00:22:16,521 --> 00:22:19,941
You guys are the witnesses!

253
00:22:20,021 --> 00:22:21,401
Yeah!

254
00:22:21,481 --> 00:22:24,151
You did it!

255
00:22:24,231 --> 00:22:27,451
That bastard... How dare he...

256
00:22:27,531 --> 00:22:29,701
Yeah! You can do it!

257
00:22:36,121 --> 00:22:37,501
Thorfinn.

258
00:22:38,541 --> 00:22:41,711
If you win, I'll let him go.

259
00:22:41,791 --> 00:22:44,251
I'll even give you a horse.

260
00:22:46,381 --> 00:22:49,381
This time isn't going to be like in London.

261
00:22:50,551 --> 00:22:53,431
Oh, I'm looking forward to that,

262
00:22:53,511 --> 00:22:55,311
son of Thors!

263
00:23:05,821 --> 00:23:08,821
The last in a line of warriors!
